        {
          "path": "_m/d/n/5/b/swan-house-atlanta-wp/historic-swan-house-1928-with-.jpg",
          "filename": "Historic Swan House (1928) with Hudson Super-Six Coach in Atlanta’s West Paces Ferry neighborhood.jpg",
          "caption": "Entrance façade of the Swan House, a 1928 mansion designed by architect Philip Trammell Shutze for Edward Inman, located in Atlanta’s Buckhead neighborhood. The house is part of the Atlanta History Center complex, though the institution is not visible in this view. A classic Hudson Super-Six Coach stands at left on the circular drive, evoking the style of the late 1920s.",
